# Frontend i18n

Never ship hardcoded user-facing copy. Use `next-intl`.

## Locales

- Files: `frontend/locales/{fr,en,ar}/common.json`
- Add every new key to **all three** locale files in the same shape
- Client: `useTranslations('namespace')`
- Server: `getTranslations('namespace')`

## Do

```tsx
const t = useTranslations('admin.products')
const tCommon = useTranslations('common')

<LayoutWrapper title={t('title')} subTitle={t('subtitle')} />
<Button text={tCommon('cancel')} />
<Label variant={EVariantLabel.bodySmall}>{t('fields.price')}</Label>
```

## Don't

```tsx
<LayoutWrapper title="Produits" subTitle="Gérer le catalogue" />
<Button text="Annuler" />
<label>Email</label>
```

## Namespaces (common.json)

| Area | Namespaces |
| --- | --- |
| Shared | `common`, `auth`, `status`, `sidebar`, `dashboard`, `errors`, `navigation` |
| Admin | `admin.*` (users, products, productCategories, testimonials, faqs, …) |
| Sales | `sales.*` (clients, quotes, invoices) |
| Shop | `shop`, `cart` |
| Marketing | `home`, `nav`, `hero`, `contact`, `footer`, `aboutUs`, `coworkingSpace`, `blog`, `faqPage`, `testimonialForm`, … |

Prefer nested keys under an existing namespace (`admin.products.fields.title`) over new top-level roots unless the feature is large.

## Allowed to stay literal

- Brand name `Biblio Squad`
- Emails, phone numbers, URLs
- Technical IDs, enum values, route paths, currency codes in formatters
